## DATA QUALITY CAVEATS — DOCUMENT THESE, DON'T HIDE THEM

- **Indices of Deprivation measure area-level relative deprivation**, NOT individual household deprivation. Using LSOA-level scores as proxies for household circumstances risks the **ecological fallacy** — acknowledge this explicitly rather than pretend it doesn't exist.
- **EPC data is known to diverge from metered energy.** Use the model for **relative prioritisation with explicit explanation** (SHAP), NOT for absolute consumption prediction.
- **Coverage bias in EPCs** — properties without a triggered cert are missing entirely.
- **Assessor error and performance-gap research** (Hardy & Glew 2019, DESNZ data) is the justification for program 2 (data-quality screening).

