## THE INTEGRATION LOOP — THE ACADEMIC HEART

This is the dissertation's central technical claim. Get it working:

1. Dashboard (Streamlit) loads merged dataset, user selects a candidate LSOA cohort
2. Calls AI service → returns ranked scores + SHAP explanations for that cohort
3. Dashboard displays the ranking; user "decides" (or the demo auto-decides) to pursue a retrofit in that LSOA
4. Decision is appended to the ledger (with synthetic grant/works data)
5. A verification outcome is later appended (simulated retrofit results)
6. SQLite state is updated with the verified outcome
7. **Next time the dashboard loads or refreshes, the write-back is visible** — the LSOA's priority or data state has changed based on real-world (simulated) feedback
8. This closed loop — not visual polish — is what makes it a "digital twin" rather than a static dashboard

**Do not skip the write-back step. It is not decoration; it is the proof that integration happened.**

